      "writtenOn": "2020-10-29T06:55:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually chip_i2c_* code is used for i2c master implementation, like chip/stm/i2c-stm32f0, chip/npcx/i2c and so on. So chip in this context is usually uC being the only master on the bus.\n\nGL3590 is a slave device, thus I don\u0027t think that master-specific i2c compilation unit is a good place to put such quirk (actually I should do this for every uC then).\n\nThat being said, it wasn\u0027t a trivial task to select the proper layer in EC i2c stack to put such a change. I selected top level i2c-master, which is common for all the masters regardless its type.",
      "parentUuid": "02b1143c_c3fca89e",
      "revId": "0a899f1a81de08a2b5e42e04e014ee19cc06d89e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
